$ exit 0
--- stdout
gh pj-synker add [<number>]... [options]
Add eligible issues and pull requests to a project

Arguments:
  [<number>]...  Issue or pull request numbers, or use --all

Options:
  --all                     Check every item in the repositories
  --author <LOGINS>         Only add items by these authors (default: any)
  --bots                    Include items by bot accounts (default: false)
  --config <FILE>           Config file to read (default: found automatically)
  --drafts                  Include draft pull requests (default: false)
  --dry-run                 Show what would be added, without adding
  --exclude-label <LABELS>  Skip items that have any of these labels
  --json                    Print the result as JSON on stdout
  --label <LABELS>          Only add items that have all of these labels
  --no-config               Don't read a config file
  --owner <LOGIN>           Project owner: user or organization
  --project <NUMBER>        Project number from its URL
  -R, --repo <REPOS>        OWNER/REPO list (default: current repository)
  --state <STATES>          Item states: open, closed (default: open)
  --type <TYPES>            Item types: issue, pull-request (default: both)
  -y, --yes                 Confirm adding the items found with --all

Global Options:
  See `gh pj-synker --help`

Examples:
  Add an issue to the project set in the config file
    gh pj-synker add 42

  Add an issue to a project without a config file
    gh pj-synker add 42 --owner acme --project 1

  Preview which triaged items would be added
    gh pj-synker add --all --label triaged --dry-run

  Add every eligible item in CI and read the result
    gh pj-synker add --all --yes --json

Notes:
  --owner and --project are required unless the config file sets them.
  Options override the config file. See gh pj-synker config check --help.
  Lists are comma-separated, such as --label triaged,accepted.
  Matching ignores case. An excluded label wins over a required label.
  Items are only added. Nothing is removed, archived, or written back.
  Items already in the project are reported as unchanged, never duplicated.
  The repository comes from --repo, GH_REPO, the config file, the current
  git checkout, then GITHUB_REPOSITORY.
  Authentication uses gh auth login, or GH_TOKEN in CI.
  The token needs the project scope.

Learn more: https://github.com/UtakataKyosui/gh-pj-synker#readme
--- stderr
